# 12-sky-fast: the stars and cloud banks of drawSkyObjects, the same pixels for less work (after 04-hills-bg).
#
# Stars: each one's hash and its row (a division by 60) depend only on its number: worked out once. Clouds: a bank's row
# widths were a division a row each (now one per bank row pair), every row went through hl/pset with the hills clip tested
# a pixel at a time (gfx_hline), and the loop ran from the cartridge (4-5 cycles an instruction). Now a bank is one IWRAM
# function (cloudBank): the rows above the highest hill top under the bank (gba_clipY, from mn[], or all of them when the
# bank is above every hill: gba_clipMin, set by hbgPrep) are plain: one span and the dithered ends straight into the row;
# banks wholly off screen are skipped; the rows a hill covers are drawn the game's way (cloudRowSlow). Checked against the
# game's own loop every frame (a check build: old and new from the same framebuffer): 0 pixels differ. (The first version
# of this patch differed from the game's loop in rare rows: an end of a 1-wide row spills a pixel past its columns.)

